---
/**
 * Opener — the top of the home page, which since D29 is the PITCH, not a
 * welcome hub, and since D113 carries BOTH halves of the claim in one screen.
 *
 * ── WHAT D113 CHANGED, AND THE ONE THING IT DELIBERATELY DID NOT ────────────
 *
 * The 2026-09-12 competitive sweep found two positions unclaimed in these
 * counties and nationally: nobody selling software here claims to have
 * personally RUN the operation it is for, and nobody lets a buyer USE the thing
 * before paying. Those are not two options to choose between — they are two
 * halves of one claim, and this band now carries both: the run of trades on the
 * left, a finished tool on the right.
 *
 * ── THE HEADLINE: I GOT THIS WRONG ONCE, AND THE RECORD IS WORTH KEEPING ────
 *
 * The first build of D113 kept the six-trade line as the h1 and REFUSED the
 * arrangement in the preview the operator had just approved. The reasoning was
 * that D33 makes that headline the positioning, that `PICKUP.md` records him
 * twice declining to reopen it, and that approving a whole-page mockup is not
 * the same act as reversing a decision.
 *
 * Every one of those statements is true and the conclusion was still wrong. He
 * answered it in one sentence: "I wanted the font, size, thickness, and
 * verbiage to match the A+C artifact, that was a main choosing point." He had
 * not overlooked the headline in the mockup — it was the thing he was choosing.
 * A concern raised once and answered is his call, and the second-guessing cost
 * him a build.
 *
 * SO THE ARRANGEMENT IS THE PREVIEW'S: the claim as the h1 in `.statement`
 * (Fraunces at weight 500 with its optical-size and wonk axes driven), the six
 * trades directly under it as the serif line that qualifies it, then the
 * operator line. Nothing about the trades is lost; what moved is which sentence
 * is the h1.
 *
 * ⚠️ THE CLAIM IS ALSO `/bio/`'s H1 WORD FOR WORD, and that duplicate is real
 * rather than theoretical — home.ts's `visionLead` comment exists to warn about
 * it. He asked for this verbiage HERE, so the duplicate has to break on the
 * other page, and that is a copy decision sitting with him.
 *
 * THE PULL-QUOTE CAME OUT, which is what pays for the band added below. The
 * preview did not have it and the hero was stating one claim three times.
 *
 * THE SCREENSHOT IS DESKTOP-ONLY, AND THAT IS MEASURED RATHER THAN TASTE. With
 * it left in on a phone the column stacks, the shot lands under the copy, and
 * the page came out 740px longer. Below 900px it is dropped here and the tools
 * band one section down carries it, so it renders exactly once at every width.
 */
import Button from '../Button.astro';
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import { versioned } from '../../data/asset-version';
import { opener, localPortal, leadOffer } from '../../data/home';
import { Store, ArrowRight } from '@lucide/astro';
---
<section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
  <div class="accent-glow -z-10"></div>

  <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-[84rem] px-6 pt-12 pb-12 sm:pt-16 sm:pb-16">
    <p class="mono-label inline-flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="status-dot"></span>
      {opener.label}
    </p>

    <div class="mt-5 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] lg:items-start lg:gap-14">
      <div>
        {/* THE ARRANGEMENT IS THE OPERATOR'S PICK, MATCHED TO THE PREVIEW.
            Claim as the h1 in the statement voice, the six trades as the serif
            line that qualifies it, then the operator line. `.statement` carries
            the font, the size and the weight; home.ts carries the verbiage. */}
        <h1 class="statement max-w-[17ch]">{opener.claim}</h1>

        <p class="statement-sub mt-4 max-w-2xl">{opener.headline}</p>

        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          {opener.operatorLine}
        </p>

        {/* THE PULL-QUOTE IS GONE, and it is a cut rather than an oversight.
            The preview he chose did not have it, and the hero was stating the
            same claim three times — headline, operator line, quote — which is
            D102's own "cut words" with the redundancy sitting in plain view.
            `visionLead` and `visionAccent` are NOT deleted from home.ts: they
            are the site's clearest statement of the argument and belong
            somewhere, which is a placement decision rather than a deletion. */}

        {/* THE ORDER OF THESE TWO REVERSED AT D113. It led with the free
            conversation — a phone call with a stranger, which the research found
            is the highest-friction step on the site. The openable thing leads
            now, and the conversation is still right beside it. */}
        <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <Button href={leadOffer.cta.href} variant="primary">{leadOffer.cta.label}</Button>
          <Button href="/contact/?intent=consult" variant="secondary">Start with a free conversation</Button>
        </div>

        {/* The local doorway (D29). The tile stays WARM (brass) because every
            other accent here is cool, and the warmth is what makes it read as a
            different KIND of thing rather than one more link. */}
        <div class="mt-6 max-w-md">
          <a href="/main-street/" class="tile-portal spotlight group flex items-center gap-4 p-4">
            <span class="grid h-11 w-11 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg border border-teal/30 bg-canvas text-brass transition-colors duration-200 group-hover:border-teal/60">
              <Store size={20} aria-hidden="true" />
            </span>
            <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
              <span class="mono-label text-cyan-deep transition-colors duration-200 group-hover:text-cyan">{localPortal.eyebrow}</span>
              <span class="mt-0.5 block font-display font-semibold text-ink">{localPortal.title}</span>
            </span>
            <ArrowRight
              size={18}
              class="shrink-0 text-brass transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:translate-x-0.5"
              aria-hidden="true"
            />
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* The proof half. Hidden below 900px — see the header. */}
      <div class="hidden lg:block">
        <a href={leadOffer.cta.href} class="block">
          <img
            src={versioned(leadOffer.shot)}
            width="1200"
            height="630"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
            alt={leadOffer.shotAlt}
            class="w-full rounded-xl border border-line shadow-2xl shadow-black/30"
          />
        </a>
        <p class="mono-label mt-3">Open this one now · no login · nothing leaves your browser</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
